ImageViewer patch (docs/PLAN.md section 15, D-57): a damaged HEIF item is an error, not an exception out of open()
Library: openimageio 3.2.1.1
Fixes: none in OSV (found by our fuzz smoke test, CI run 80)
Upstream: AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenImageIO #5556, on main after 3.2.1.3 (ours, upstreamed)
Remove when: a release contains #5556 (the update script removes a patch the release already contains)

A heif::Error escaped open() for a HEIF item without properties and aborted the viewer on all
three systems (0.4). Test: tests/fuzz_smoke.py.

diff --git a/src/heif.imageio/heifinput.cpp b/src/heif.imageio/heifinput.cpp
index 8f18db4..d631e12 100644
--- a/src/heif.imageio/heifinput.cpp
+++ b/src/heif.imageio/heifinput.cpp
@@ -287,8 +287,16 @@ bool
 HeifInput::read_subimage_spec(int subimage)
 {
     // m_item_ids[0] is the primary image; the rest follow in file order.
-    auto id   = m_item_ids[subimage];
-    m_ihandle = m_ctx->get_image_handle(id);
+    auto id = m_item_ids[subimage];
+    try {
+        m_ihandle = m_ctx->get_image_handle(id);
+    } catch (const heif::Error& err) {
+        // A damaged file (e.g. an item without properties): an error, not
+        // an exception escaping open() and terminating the program.
+        std::string e = err.get_message();
+        errorfmt("{}", e.empty() ? "unknown exception" : e.c_str());
+        return false;
+    }
 
     m_bitdepth = m_ihandle.get_luma_bits_per_pixel();
     if (m_bitdepth < 0) {
